we can distribute the scalar multiplication and then subtract the two vectors component-wise:
\begin{align*}
3 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix} - 2 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} 3 \cdot 2 \\ 3 \cdot -8 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 2 \cdot 1 \\ 2 \cdot -7 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -24 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -14 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 6 - 2 \\ -24 - (-14) \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
