Let
\[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x + 3 & \text{if $x < 20$}, \\
2x - 2 & \text{if $x \ge 20$}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find $f^{-1}(7) + f^{-1}(46).$

solution_steps:
We can rewrite $\sqrt{7}$ as $7^{1/2}$.
Using the property of logarithms that $\log_a b^c = c\log_a b$, we have $\log_7 \sqrt{7} = \log_7 7^{1/2} = \frac{1}{2}\log_7 7 = \frac{1}{2}\cdot 1 = \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}$.
The answer is: \frac{1}{2}

